---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import SceneFrame from "./SceneFrame.astro";
import { scene } from "../lib/scenes";
const covers = ["daisy-starting", "daisy-teaching", "daisy-whiteboard", "daisy-brb"].map(scene);
const swatches = ["#16181e", "#e8a33d", "#f4f5f7"];
---
<section class="section mist" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
      <p class="lede">Set up your views once. Then every show is a click away, and OBS keeps streaming the way it always does.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <div class="vis setup" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="field"><span>Show name</span><b>Intro to Watercolor</b></div>
          <div class="field"><span>This week</span><b>Wet-on-wet skies</b></div>
          <div class="field"><span>Colors</span><i class="sw">{swatches.map((c) => <i style={`background:${c}`}></i>)}</i></div>
        </div>
        <h3><span class="n">1</span>Pick your views</h3>
        <p>Start from a designed set of views, then put in your show's name, your colors and this week's title.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="vis tiles on-dark" aria-hidden="true">
          {covers.map((c, i) => (
            <div class:list={["tile", { live: i === 1 }]}>
              <Picture src={c.image} alt="" widths={[240, 360]} sizes="10rem" formats={["webp"]} fallbackFormat="jpg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              {i === 1 && <span class="badge"><i class="dot"></i>On air</span>}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <h3><span class="n">2</span>Click to switch</h3>
        <p>Click a view in the Mac app, in any browser, or on a phone or tablet beside you.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="vis"><SceneFrame id="daisy-teaching" alt="A teaching view on air, with the camera and the screen share in their places" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, calc(100vw - 2.5rem)" /></div>
        <h3><span class="n">3</span>Everything moves into place</h3>
        <p>Your camera, screen share and titles land where the view puts them, and OBS keeps streaming as usual. Nothing to rebuild for each layout.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 3rem 2rem; }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) { .steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .steps li { display: grid; gap: 0.85rem; align-content: start; }
  .steps p { color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 30rem; }
  h3 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .n { font: 700 0.9375rem/1 var(--display); color: var(--ink-3); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .vis { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; }
  .vis :global(.frame) { height: 100%; aspect-ratio: auto; border-radius: 14px; }
  .setup { background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1rem 1.1rem; display: grid; align-content: center; gap: 0.55rem; }
  .field { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .field span { color: var(--ink-3); }
  .field b { font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  .sw { display: flex; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .sw i { width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; border-radius: 50%; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #0000001f; }
  .tiles { background: var(--monitor); padding: 1rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-content: center; }
  .tile { position: relative; }
  .tile :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; border-radius: 6px; outline: 2px solid transparent; outline-offset: 2px; }
  .tile.live :global(img) { outline-color: var(--live); }
  .badge { position: absolute; left: 0.4rem; bottom: 0.4rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; background: var(--monitor); color: var(--on-monitor); font: 600 0.75rem/1 var(--text); padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; }
  .dot { width: 0.45rem; height: 0.45rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--live); display: inline-block; }
</style>
